  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "If $x=\\sqrt{2}-1$ and $y=\\sqrt{3}+1$, find:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$xy$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}-1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}xy&=(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{3}+1)\\\\xy&=\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x+y$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x+y&=(\\sqrt{2}-1)+(\\sqrt{3}+1)\\\\x+y&=\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x(x+2)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x(x+2)&=(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)\\\\x(x+2)&=2+\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}-1\\\\x(x+2)&=1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{3}x-\\sqrt{2}y$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{3}x-\\sqrt{2}y&=\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{2}-1)-\\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{3}+1)\\\\\\sqrt{3}x-\\sqrt{2}y&=\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}\\\\\\sqrt{3}x-\\sqrt{2}y&=-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$2xy$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt{6}+2\\sqrt{2}-2\\sqrt{3}-2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2xy&=2(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{3}+1)\\\\2xy&=2(\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}-1)\\\\2xy&=2\\sqrt{6}+2\\sqrt{2}-2\\sqrt{3}-2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x+3y$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{2}+3\\sqrt{3}+2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x+3y&=(\\sqrt{2}-1)+3(\\sqrt{3}+1)\\\\x+3y&=\\sqrt{2}+3\\sqrt{3}+2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$(x+1)(y+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{6}+2\\sqrt{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)(y+1)&=\\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{3}+2)\\\\(x+1)(y+1)&=\\sqrt{6}+2\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{6\\sqrt{10}}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6\\sqrt{5}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6\\sqrt{10}}{x+1}&=\\frac{6\\sqrt{10}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\\\frac{6\\sqrt{10}}{x+1}&=6\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{2}}\\\\\\frac{6\\sqrt{10}}{x+1}&=6\\sqrt{5}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{x}+\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt{2}$\n\nExpand $(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)$ to identify the reciprocals.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)&=2+\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}-1\\\\(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\dfrac{1}{x}=\\sqrt{2}+1$ and $\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}=\\sqrt{2}-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}&=(\\sqrt{2}+1)+(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\\\\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}&=2\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{x}-\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$\n\nExpand $(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)$ to identify the reciprocals.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)&=2+\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}-1\\\\(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\dfrac{1}{x}=\\sqrt{2}+1$ and $\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}=\\sqrt{2}-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}&=(\\sqrt{2}+1)-(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\\\\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}&=2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q7-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$x+\\dfrac{1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt{2}$\n\nUse $(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)=1$ to identify $\\frac{1}{x}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)&=2+\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}-1\\\\(\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{2}+1)&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\dfrac{1}{x}=\\sqrt{2}+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac{1}{x}&=(\\sqrt{2}-1)+(\\sqrt{2}+1)\\\\x+\\frac{1}{x}&=2\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
